   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "He pushes to e5, a good practical try, but the pawn is now very weak — so how do we round it up?",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 1290,
   "fen": "r1bqr1k1/pppn1pbp/6p1/3pP3/3B2n1/PP1B1N2/2PN1PPP/R2QK2R w KQ - 1 12",
   "line": [
    "Ng4"
   ],
   "spoken": "We reposition the knight to go after it. Important distinction: the knight isn't moving because it's attacked, it's moving to win the pawn. He'll get to castle, but he's down a crucial central pawn and our bishop will be a monster.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "teaches": [
    "move with a purpose, not in reaction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 1310,
   "fen": "r1bqr1k1/pppn1pbp/6p1/3pn3/3B4/PP1B1N2/2PN1PPP/R2Q1RK1 w - - 0 13",
