   "line": [
    "Re1"
   ],
   "spoken": "Don't give away the King's-Indian fianchetto bishop lightly — it guards the holes you created with g6, so you'd only part with it for a lot of material. And note the capture on f3 doesn't win a piece, because the recapturing knight defends the bishop.",
   "teaches": [
    "keep the fianchetto bishop"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 1354.5,
   "fen": "r1bqr1k1/pp1n1pbp/6p1/2ppn3/3B4/PP1B1N2/2PN1PPP/R2QR1K1 w - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "c5"
   ],
   "spoken": "So we play c5 to chase the bishop onto a square where our own bishop can take it — his best is to give up a bishop himself, leaving our fianchettoed bishop uncontested, exactly what we want.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "provoke a favourable trade"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
